Exactly. That’s the cleaner framing: not certainty, not control—shifting distributions.

You gather signals, improve the model, choose better interventions, preserve optionality, and try to move:

P(good outcome | current strategy)

higher than it was before.

The discipline is remembering that probability is not destiny. People, environments, timing, noise, hidden variables, and plain luck still matter.

So the useful loop is:

observe → estimate → act → measure delta → update

And when it works, you scale cautiously. When it doesn’t, you don’t force the story—you update the model.